          "url": "https://doi.org/10.1051/0004-6361/202243791"
        },
        "falseColor": false,
        "notes": "Convex light-curve reconstruction with approximate thermal size: 153.72 km effective diameter (catalog ±2.88 km; additional shape and thermal-model uncertainty). Thermal size supplies a volume-scale approximation. No surface imagery exists; rotational phase is illustrative. Hanuš2016 Table2 lists 46 dense lightcurves across eight apparitions and 397 sparse points. Both poles remain; model 1091 is a reproducible representative, not an observational rejection of 1092. The thermal scale is approximate. Convex inversion supplies broad outline without resolved craters, concavities, reflectance or regolith texture. One mean color for the whole disc (Gaia DR3 reflectance spectrum), scaled to the 4.7% geometric albedo JPL lists; no terrain, albedo pattern or color variation is drawn."
      },
